-- title:
--   A cyclic generator-kernel polynomial splits over ⟨ Q⟩
-- statement:
--   Let $\Omega$ be an algebraically closed field with decidable equality, let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ that is elliptic, let $p$ be a prime and $k$ a natural number, and assume $p \neq 0$ in $\Omega$ and $3 \le p^k$. Let $h \in \Omega[X]$ satisfy `W.IsCyclicGenKernel p k h`, that is: $\deg h \le \varphi(p^k)/2$ (natural-number division), the coefficient of $h$ in degree $\varphi(p^k)/2$ is $1$ (so $h$ is monic of that exact degree), the product $h \cdot \mathrm{pre}\Psi_{p^{k-1}}$ divides $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{p^k}$, and for every natural $a$ with $2 \le a \le (p^k-1)/2$ and $p \nmid a$ the polynomial $h$ divides $\sum_{i \le d} h_i\, \Phi_a^{\,i}\, \Psi\mathrm{Sq}_a^{\,d-i}$, where $d = \varphi(p^k)/2$ and $h_i$ are the coefficients of $h$ (the $a$-scaling numerator of $h$). Let $Q$ be a point of the affine model of $W$ of exact additive order $p^k$, and assume that $Q$ is an affine point $(x,y)$ with $x$ a root of $h$. Then $$h = \prod_{\substack{1 \le a \le p^k/2 \\ p \nmid a}} \bigl(X - x(aQ)\bigr),$$ where $x(\cdot)$ denotes the first component of `coordsOrZero`, which sends the point at infinity to $(0,0)$ and an affine point $(x,y)$ to $(x,y)$.
--
--   The statement identifies a cyclic generator-kernel polynomial of level $p^k$ with the kernel polynomial of the cyclic subgroup generated by any point whose abscissa it annihilates; in particular such a polynomial is determined by one of its roots. It is used in the construction of $\Gamma_0(p^k)$- and $\Gamma_1$-level data on Weierstrass curves over algebraically closed fields, for instance in producing cyclic subgroups of order $p^k$ from generator-kernel polynomials and in comparing such data under variable changes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_IsCyclicGenKernel_eq_prod_X_sub_C_coordsOrZero_nsmul.lean

